# Build
/target/
Cargo.lock

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Config (may contain secrets). Anchored: unanchored, this also matched
# `.cargo/config.toml`, which is tracked and must stay visible.
/config.toml

# Local database. SQLite writes `-wal` and `-shm` beside the `.db`, and neither
# suffix is matched by `*.db`. `/data/` is the running till's state directory,
# ignored as a whole so a new sidecar suffix does not have to be chased.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
/data/

# Logs
*.log
wadi-pos-terminal-linux

# Vendored Rust deps (offline builds only; do not track)
/vendor/
*.tar.gz

# Migration backup dirs
*.bak/

# Local worktrees (used by EnterWorktree)
.worktrees/

# Agent-session state. Scoped rather than a blanket `.claude/`, so shared agent
# configuration (skills, commands) can still be tracked if it is ever wanted.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.superpowers/

# The pact consumer crate resolves its own graph outside the workspace.
# `pacts/` is deliberately NOT ignored: the artifact is the reviewable record of
# what the till expects, and it is copied into the platform repository from here.
/crates/pos-contract/target/
# The lock IS committed, against the repo-wide `Cargo.lock` rule three lines up.
# The generated pact embeds its resolver versions (`metadata.pactRust`), so an
# unpinned graph makes the artifact change without anyone changing an expectation
# — and a diff that is noisy every time is a diff nobody reads.
!/crates/pos-contract/Cargo.lock
